A||||9||Ronen||Removing the seats||||8||
Z||000000||Ronen||05-24-2001||04:44 PM||||Removing the two front nuts and the one next to the passenger door were easy enough. But, how do I remove the fourth nut that holds the seat down in the back against the center consol?||||reg||8
Z||000001||DecadenceR||05-24-2001||04:46 PM||||When i did that, I used a regular box-end wrench. And WD-40. It took a while, but I couldn't get anything else in there. You may have to hook another wrench on the end of it to give you some leverage though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||05-24-2001||04:50 PM||||do you have the seat pushed all the way forward, and tilted forward all the way?<P>I didnt have any trouble taking my seats out to clean the carpet.<P>  one mechanics trick to take off nuts you cant get a wrench on is to use a chisel and hammer. Put the chisel slightly off center, and when you wack it a few times the nut will either unscrew or split.<P>   either way, its off. You can put them back on the same way, and get them pretty tight without splitting them. They only split coming off if they were hopelessly rusted on anyway - in which case you would have twisted the stud off with a wrench.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-24-2001||04:54 PM||||I believe the nuts are 13mm.  I have never had a problem getting them off.  I used a racheting box end wrench (Ace Gear Wrench), so I didnt have to keep taking off and repositioning a regular box end wrench.  You can get the Gear Wrench at either Ace Hardware stores or I believe Craftsman has their own version. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||05-24-2001||05:19 PM||||With the seat all the way forward and tilted all the way forward, I have no trouble getting a ratchet and shallow socket on the nut.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ronen||05-24-2001||06:24 PM||||I just tried moving the seat forward in the passenger side of my spare Fiero and yes it is easily reachable. The problem is that I tried moving the seat forward on my good Fiero and it is, I guess, stuck. Any suggestions? Should I take a small hammer to it?||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroFanaticus2||05-24-2001||06:26 PM||||The seats in an '86 Coupe I had were easy to remove with a ratchet and socket, but the ones in my '88 coupe were more difficult and I ended up using a set of adjustable locking pliers.  It took some time and a lot of swearing, but eventually it came out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||KRMFiero||05-24-2001||06:51 PM||||Yes bolts are 13mm, just use a wrench to take them off, takes a while but it works  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||05-24-2001||07:57 PM||||slide it all way forward to take out rear 2, all the back to get front 2, i just use ratchet and socket.||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroBUZZ||05-24-2001||08:54 PM||||The seatbelt arm and bolt on the tunnel tend to bind the seat.  If it's just non use then the track should loosen with some WD-40 and moving it back and forth.<BR>Gary||||reg||3
